<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/05UR">Example <span data-tag="05UR">7.7.3.11</span>.</a> Let $\operatorname{QCat}$ denote the (cartesian closed) category of (small) $\infty $-categories (Example <a data-tag="05UH" href="/tag/05UH">7.7.3.3</a>). Let us regard $\operatorname{QCat}$ as equipped with the simplicial enrichment given in Construction <a data-tag="0209" href="/tag/0209">5.5.3.1</a>, with morphism spaces given by the formula </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \operatorname{Hom}_{\operatorname{QCat}}( \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}, \operatorname{\mathcal{D}})_{\bullet } = \operatorname{Fun}( \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}, \operatorname{\mathcal{D}})^{\simeq }. \]
</div>
<p> This simplicial enrichment satisfies the hypotheses of Remark <a data-tag="05UP" href="/tag/05UP">7.7.3.9</a>, so the $\infty $-category $\operatorname{\mathcal{QC}}= \operatorname{N}_{\bullet }^{\operatorname{hc}}( \operatorname{QCat})$ is cartesian closed. </p>
</article>
